# Bootstrap Protocol Overview

Spec: Bootstrap
Purpose:
  Define the AI entry point — what AI reads and resolves when entering
  a .sdd project. The bootstrap protocol ensures deterministic, minimum-
  sufficient context loading without scanning the entire .sdd/ directory.

  AI does NOT read entire .sdd/. AI resolves context through the
  Context Compiler using index-first, progressive disclosure.

Owns: bootstrap/

## The Bootstrap Protocol (AI_BOOTSTRAP.v1)

  1.  WHO AM I?           → Read identity.sdd — project, role, capabilities
  2.  AUTHORITY CHECK     → Read authority.sdd — what AI can/cannot do
  3.  MANDATORY RULES     → Read protocol/ROOT.sdd — immutable system rules
  4.  PROJECT RESOLVE     → Resolve project from INDEX.sdd → PROJECT_INDEX
  5.  INDEX RESOLVE       → Resolve domain/task/plan indexes
  6.  ARCHITECTURE        → Load current architecture version
  7.  GLOSSARY RESOLVE    → Load mandatory terms + domain terms on demand
  8.  TASK RESOLVE        → Resolve current task from task index
  9.  KNOWLEDGE RESOLVE   → Load active decisions, required skills, references
  10. ASSUMPTION CHECK   → Inspect unknowns, risk levels, blocking status
  11. READINESS GATE     → Validate all gates pass before execution
  12. CONTEXT COMPILE    → Compile minimum sufficient context via Context Compiler
  13. EXECUTE            → Begin work within authority limits

## Authority Model

  AI MUST check authority before any executing action.

  CAN:
    read-code, modify-code, run-tests, create-tasks, propose-skills

  CANNOT:
    change-global-rules, approve-production, modify-security-policy

  Full authority model: @authority.sdd

## Mandatory Rules Priority

  1. Correctness    (never compromise correctness)
  2. Security       (never bypass security constraints)
  3. Architecture   (respect architecture constraints)
  4. KISS           (keep it simple when possible)
  5. DRY            (avoid duplication when simple)
  6. YAGNI          (don't add what isn't needed)

## Navigation Protocol

  AI follows index-first resolution:

  AI_BOOTSTRAP
    → ROOT INDEX
    → PROJECT INDEX
    → DOMAIN INDEX
    → TASK INDEX
    → RELEVANT REFERENCES

  Never scan a collection when an index can resolve the required context.

## Progressive Disclosure

  Context is loaded in layers (see: @../system/context/INDEX.sdd):

  LEVEL 0:  metadata
  LEVEL 1:  summary
  LEVEL 2:  rules
  LEVEL 3:  implementation details
  LEVEL 4:  evidence/source

  AI loads only the level needed for current work.

## Readiness Gates

  G1: Project resolved
  G2: Task resolved
  G3: Architecture resolved
  G4: Required skills resolved
  G5: Critical assumptions resolved
  G6: Permissions valid

  If any gate fails → STATUS: NOT_READY → AI does NOT execute.

## Bootstrap Modes

  BOOTSTRAP_IMPL      — for implementation tasks
  BOOTSTRAP_REVIEW    — for code review
  BOOTSTRAP_RESEARCH — for research/exploration
  BOOTSTRAP_RELEASE  — for release/deployment

  Each mode loads different context slices.

## Context Compiler

  .sdd files (source of truth)
        ↓
  Context Compiler (progressive disclosure, priority filtering)
        ↓
  AI Context (runtime representation with manifest + diff)

  See: @../system/context/INDEX.sdd

## Handoff Protocol

  Agent-to-agent communication transfers structured state,
  not conversation history.

  See: @handoff.sdd

